 #html_wrapper_imports_end -->
 <div id="content"
   ?ntp-threads-rail-open="${this.showComposebox_ && this.enableThreadsRail_}">
+  <!-- Sunshine's New Tab background.
+       An iframe rather than an <img> or a CSS background, because the New Tab
+       page overrides child-src to admit chrome-untrusted://new-tab-page and
+       does not override img-src. That is also why upstream's own custom
+       background is an iframe, and this reuses that helper rather than
+       inventing a second way in.
+       The hidden attribute goes on whenever the document is not visible.
+       PB-5a permits this animation only while it is being looked at, and a
+       hidden subtree renders nothing, so an animated asset inside it decodes
+       nothing. Hidden rather than removed on purpose: removing it would
+       re-read the file from disk on every return to the tab, and
+       UntrustedSource does not cache.
+       No backticks anywhere in this file. It is preprocessed into a
+       TypeScript template literal, where a backtick ends the string and
+       dollar-brace starts an expression - which is why the upstream comment
+       this replaced wrote its binding as a backslash-escaped dollar. -->
+  <ntp-iframe id="sunshineBackground" src="${this.sunshineBackgroundPath_}"
+      ?hidden="${!this.sunshineBackgroundVisible_}"></ntp-iframe>
   ${this.lazyRender_ && this.microsoftModuleEnabled_ ? html`
     <iframe id="microsoftAuth" src="${this.microsoftAuthIframePath_}"></iframe>
   ` : ''}
@@ -28,13 +46,9 @@ import {SubmitButtonIconType} from '//resources/cr_components/composebox/compose
         </ntp-iframe>
         `
     ) : ''}
-  <!-- TODO(crbug.com/40743294): Instead of ?hidden="\${!this.logoEnabled_}" it would
-       be nicer to use Lit's conditional rendering. However, that breaks
